      "description": "In popular culture and online discourse, 'rez' is sometimes used as a derogatory term to refer to Indigenous people, often implying they are 'crazy,' 'uneducated,' or 'living in poverty.' This usage is rooted in racist stereotypes and is considered offensive by many Indigenous communities.",
